  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: Both completed experiments (config_001, config_006) used pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with multimodal/multiprofile/avgpool/weighted settings, yielding ~0.635-0.639 accuracy. The only tested variable was image encoder (resnet50 slightly ahead of ViT-L by 0.4%). The RNA encoder choice remains completely unexplored, and it is a fundamental representation decision that could substantially shift performance. Question: config_025 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding all other settings identical to config_001 (resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile), providing a clean single-variable ablation. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether a learned generative RNA representation (scvi) outperforms a linear one (PCA) is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact question. A positive result would justify further exploration of scvi-based configs; a null or negative result would confirm PCA sufficiency and redirect budget toward aggregation/fusion or profile-setting variations."
}

